---
kind: scanrepo
ext: .scanrepo
version: 1
mime: application/x-scanrepo
binary: false
trigger: scanrepo paper git printed repo physical software scan back
---

## Purpose

Printable master of a git snapshot. A human can read the source on the page. A phone camera recovers the same bytes through page QR codes, then a restorer rebuilds blobs, a tree, and a commit so `git checkout` matches the paper.

## Structure

1. First line is the magic banner `# scanrepo v1`
2. YAML frontmatter between `---` fences with keys: repo, edition, branch, commit, tree, parent, pages
3. One or more page blocks. Each block starts with `## PAGE <n>` and ends with `## END PAGE`
4. Inside a page block, header lines are `key: value` until a line that is exactly `text:`
5. Lines after `text:` and before `## END PAGE` are the file bytes, including blank lines
6. Required page keys: path, mode, blob, chunk, chunk_of
7. Cover identity lives only in frontmatter. File bytes live only in page blocks.

## Parse rules

- Reject the file if line 1 is not `# scanrepo v1`
- Frontmatter keys are required: repo, edition, branch, commit, tree, parent, pages
- `parent` may be the token `none`
- Page blocks must be numbered 1..pages with no gaps
- Split header lines on the first `: `
- File bytes are everything between the `text:` line and `## END PAGE`, with the trailing newline before `## END PAGE` stripped
- Rejoin chunks for the same path in chunk order before hashing
- Blob check: SHA-1 of `blob <len>\0` plus rejoined bytes must equal the `blob` field
- Tree and commit fields are git object ids; the restorer recomputes them and rejects a mismatch

## Write rules

- Always start with `# scanrepo v1`
- One edition per file. A later printing is a new file with edition bumped and parent set to the prior commit
- Never put packfiles or deltas in the body. Store full blob text
- Chunk a file only when it will not fit one printed page (about 1800 source characters)
- Hash with git blob rules, not raw SHA-1 of the file
- Page order is the recovery order. Path order inside a tree is byte-sorted, git style

## Example

See sample.scanrepo
